The files postcodes-au.tsv, postcodes-nz.tsv, postcodes-us.tsv and postcodes-gb.tsv are derived from the GeoNames
postal code downloads (https://download.geonames.org/export/zip/: AU, NZ, US and GB, downloaded 4 Nov 2026). Changes
made: one point per postcode (the average of the GeoNames rows sharing it), rounded to 3 decimal places; postcodes
tidied the way CROP stores them; US kept to 5-digit ZIP codes; the UK file holds outward codes only (e.g. "LS1").
GeoNames provides the data "as is", without warranty of accuracy, timeliness or completeness.

Regenerate with: python3 -I apps/api/scripts/build-postcodes.py <folder with AU/AU.txt, NZ/NZ.txt, US/US.txt, GB/GB.txt>

CROP uses these points only to work out an approximate straight-line distance between a worker's home postcode and
a site's postcode.
